-- title:
--   Reductions of q-expansions as chart values on the fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $M/p$ nonzero, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbf{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a proof `hj` that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the $q$-expansion function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` of the full modular group; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of the bundle `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), whose residue field $\kappa_A$ has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed, and let $\rho : R_p \to A$ be a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ is the structure map $R_p \to \overline{\mathbf{Q}}$. Write $F' =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC` $\kappa_A$ for the level group `ΓN p M H hpM`, and let $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}$ be the associated curve model over $\kappa_A$ with function field $F'$, together with its morphism $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{efib}$ to the fibre product of `toBase p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the reduction $\kappa_A$-valued map. The assertion is the conjunction of two clauses, one for the finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin` (elements of the rational $q$-expansion function field integral over the $R_p$-subalgebra generated by $j$, with chart immersion `ιFin`) and one for `chartAlgInf` (the same with $j^{-1}$, immersion `ιInf`). In each clause: for every $\kappa_A$-point $y$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}$, i.e. a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} \kappa_A \to \mathrm{Mfib}.C$ splitting its structure morphism, and every ring homomorphism $\beta$ from the chart algebra to $\kappa_A$ such that $y$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{efib}$ followed by the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\beta)$ followed by the chart immersion, and for every chart element $b$ and every Laurent series $y_b$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}((q))$ is the $q$-expansion of $b$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y_b$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ lies in $F'$, that element of $F'$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $\mathrm{Mfib}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}(y)$ attached to $y$, and its difference from the image of $\beta(b)$ under $\kappa_A \to F'$ lies in the nonunits of that valuation subring.
--
--   This supplies, for the special fibre at $p$ of the Deligne–Rapoport-style model of $X_H(M)$, the dictionary that reads each chart function at each $\kappa_A$-point through reduction of $q$-expansions: the reduced series is a function on the fibre curve, it is regular at the place of the point, and its value there is $\beta(b)$. It is used in the analysis of places of the fibre not coming from the affine charts, via [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_mem_closure_chartAlgInf_hasValue_residue_zero_and_not_hasValue_of_not_isAffinePlace_of_ne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_mem_closure_chartAlgInf_hasValue_residue_zero_and_not_hasValue_of_not_isAffinePlace_of_ne).
